Experiment B0 of the profiling case (October 2026): the WENO half-width S as a compile-time constant (SC = 3) in
compute_face_fluxes_dev, the face kernel of every FLUME model, so the stencil loops have constant bounds.

NOT a fix: the kernel then ignores the [weno] scheme of the input and is right only for WENO-5 (S = 3), the scheme of
the profiling case. Apply it to a clean tree for a variant build, revert it right after, never commit it:

  git apply src/tests/flume/speedup/profile-couette3d/patches/face-kernel-s3.patch
  cd src/tests/flume/speedup && ./build.sh fnl-nvf --varset iac_nvf --jobs 16 --tag B0-lto --gpu lto && cd -
  git apply -R src/tests/flume/speedup/profile-couette3d/patches/face-kernel-s3.patch

The results and what they mean are in ../README.md, "Results".

